audio.cpp fork delta: the VibeASR CPU INT8 / ternary pipeline, captured
2026-09-23 (previously untracked in external/ggml - see 0008's header). Source
commit: audio.cpp #447 (62a9441f, "ggml: additive INT8/ternary types, fused CPU
ops, and kernels for VibeASR (1/2)"), ported from microsoft/VibeASR.cpp.

Types (appended after the last upstream type; GGML_TYPE_COUNT grows by 2):
  - GGML_TYPE_I8_S: int8 payload plus ONE per-tensor F32 scale stored in-band
    immediately after the payload (ggml_type_extra_bytes, ggml_inband_scale in
    ggml-impl.h; ggml_nbytes accounts for it). The retired IQ4_NL_4_4/4_8 ids
    36/37 are deliberately NOT reused - reuse would misread old GGUF files.
  - GGML_TYPE_I2_S: 2-bit ternary weights in 128-element blocks.
Ops (appended at the tail of ggml_op, so GGML_OP_NAME/SYMBOL stay positional):
  ADD_SCALED, RMS_NORM_SCALED, MUL_MAT_ADD, MUL_MAT_ADD_RELU, IM2COL_ASYM - CPU
  only, the way convrot_linear / sage_attn2_i8 are CUDA only. ggml_mul_mat with
  an I2_S src0 branches to ggml_compute_forward_mul_mat_i2_s, which owns its
  activation quantization (per-row scale and int8 row sum survive to the
  epilogue). The fused ops stage their whole output in F32 (cplan work size)
  because the output scale is only known once every element exists.
Kernels: ggml_vec_dot_i8_i8 / ggml_vec_dot_i2_i8 (AVX2 and NEON dotprod paths,
scalar tail); quantize/dequantize rows for both types in ggml-quants.c. A dup
of an I8_S tensor carries the in-band scale across (read through view_src for
permuted views), since a byte copy alone would leave it uninitialised.

Consumer: src/community_models/vibeasr. This patch edits the type and op
tables, so expect to rebase it on every ggml bump that appends types or ops:
keep I8_S/I2_S and the five ops AFTER whatever upstream appends.

